118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (The whole bus \(and the floor-2 hub\) is one collision domain at 10 Mbps shared by 30 PCs. Everyone is half-duplex and CSMA/CD collisions waste capacity. Average share = 10/30 = 0.33 Mbps. Example: 5 people saving at once with ~40% usable capacity = 4 Mbps / 5 = 0.8 Mbps each, so a 10 MB file \(80 Mbit\) takes 80 / 0.8 = 100 s. The server is at the far end of the same shared cable.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (One home router does everything \(routing, NAT, DHCP, Wi-Fi\) and is the only path out, so it's a single point of failure. There's no firewall or second path, and a restart takes the whole office offline.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
