/T (Moving a desk: every desk now has its own cable to a switch, so one change touches one port only. Slow saves: each PC gets a dedicated 1 Gbps full-duplex link instead of sharing 10 Mbps, and the server has a 2 Gbps trunk. Router restarts: a separate firewall/router and switch mean the LAN, server and printer keep working even while the internet is restarting. Also removed: collisions, a single point of failure on the cable, and guests reaching staff PCs \(VLANs\). \(82 words\))
/E (Moving a desk: every desk now has its own cable to a switch, so one change touches one port only. Slow saves: each PC gets a dedicated 1 Gbps full-duplex link instead of sharing 10 Mbps, and the server has a 2 Gbps trunk. Router restarts: a separate firewall/router and switch mean the LAN, server and printer keep working even while the internet is restarting. Also removed: collisions, a single point of failure on the cable, and guests reaching staff PCs \(VLANs\). \(82 words\))
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
